    "definitions": {
      "balance_median_ratio": "median over the independent rows i of S of |(Sv)_i| / (omega_i + balance_epsilon), with omega_i = 0.5 sum_j |S_ij v_j| the layer's own turnover. This is FluxLayer.forward's feas_balance_median, per sample instead of batch-reduced.",
      "balance_max_ratio": "the same ratio, maximized over the independent rows.",
      "box_violation_frac": "fraction of the 4,131 reactions with v > ub + 1e-4 or v < lb - 1e-4, where (lb, ub) is FluxLayer.dynamic_box at this sample's availability and abundance. The box parameterization satisfies this by construction, so a nonzero value is a bug rather than an infeasibility.",
      "thermo_model_violation_frac": "fraction of active reactions (delta_r_g0_mask and not thermo_exempt) with v * delta_r_G > thermo_epsilon, using the layer's OWN delta_r_G from reaction_potential, which includes the learned concentration term. Available only when the arm's thermo_mode is not OFF.",
      "thermo_model_uphill_frac": "mean over active reactions of relu(v dG + eps) / (|v||dG| + eps), the per-sample form of the layer's c_thermo. Available only when thermo_mode is not OFF.",
      "thermo_standard_state_violation_frac": "fraction of active reactions with v * (delta_r_G0 + delta_r_G_transport) > thermo_epsilon. An AUDIT REFERENCE, not the layer's own term: it evaluates the second law at standard state because an arm with thermo_mode OFF learns no concentrations, so the concentration term RT S^T ln c is absent rather than zero.",
      "thermo_standard_state_uphill_frac": "the same standard-state driving force in the c_thermo normalization.",
      "fractions": "fraction of the genotypes in the group meeting each named criterion. 'both_balance_le_1e-02_and_<thermo>_eq_0' is the Genesis criterion: mass balance within 1 percent and no uphill active reaction.",
      "rank_by": "top-100 groups are the 100 genotypes with the HIGHEST predicted betaxanthin (denormalized head mean), i.e. the strains the model nominates as producers."
